From: mscharged-port
Subject: Time the native GX pipeline's phases
Upstream-base: d664382f57002fbff143911c81b06b7e7a4b3ab4
Classification: host diagnostics, no behaviour change.

For frame logs (the Switch runs at a fraction of the desktop frame rate, and
the logs must show where a frame goes): the host can switch on totals of the
game thread's phases (drawing its views, the rest of its frame) and of its
waits at a draw-done and at the VI retrace, of the FIFO processor's parsing
and of its wait until a draw-done frame finished on the GPU, of the render
worker's work with the command buffer submit, the GPU wait, the window image
acquire and the present inside it, with thread CPU times and samples of the
CPU core each of these threads ran on. Off by default; switched off, each hook
reads one relaxed flag. Nothing waits, orders or submits differently.

